From 33c20b342f25e75857242fd6c3909c0ac2e867fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:31:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] hwcomposer: Show YUV video through an RGB copy

Apps that decode video themselves (TikTok) post YV12 buffers straight
to the hwcomposer, which sent them on as three-plane dmabufs. Marathon
neither advertises nor imports planar YUV, so it rejected the buffer
with a protocol error; the hwcomposer reconnected every half second and
every Android window went black.

Draw each YUV frame on the hwcomposer's EGL thread into a BGRA buffer
of its own and send that, linear, as ARGB8888. Where the buffer cannot
be allocated linear, convert on the CPU into SHM with libyuv instead.
That fallback costs a fifth of a core on a 576x1024 video, as it reads
uncached memory; the GPU path costs 3%.
